ect and incorrect authentication behavior, wrong-secret handling, handover integrity, and platform retention were all observed. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state, and post-restart authentication were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities. Only minor retained backup and temporary-log residue reduces operational hygiene.","limitations":["Secret and credential values are appropriately redacted; matching hashes, configuration validation, and end-to-end behavior provide strong indirect confirmation of their final consistency.","The final lifecycle inventory does not cover /etc/raddb, so continued presence of the two .legacy2-backup files is inferred from their creation and the absence of any captured cleanup command.","Post-restart wrong-secret checks prove absence of Access-Accept but do not preserve the complete radtest response; the initial probe more specifically records the response as discarded or unverifiable."]}
